{"segs": ["PA_ja_108:0.2", "PA_ja_108:0.3"], "en": "First Collection (Ekakanipāta), Chapter on the Group of One Hundred and Fifty (Parosatavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_108:0.4"], "en": "8. The Bāhiya Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_108:1.1"], "en": "One should train in those things that ought to be trained in;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_108:1.2"], "en": "there are people who possess the desire [to do so].", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_108:1.3", "PA_ja_108:1.4"], "en": "\"For by means of a good meal, Bāhiya indeed gratified the king.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_108:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the eighth Jātaka, the Bāhiya-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
